  "worked_solution": "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}\u2061x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}\u2061x+1={sec}^{2}\u2061x\\,\u27f9\\,{tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{2}\u2061x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{tan}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4({sec}^{2}\u2061x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}\u2061x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-3{x}^{2}+4{sec}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+C \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
